All local gates pass: 0/200,000 random hits, five attacks at 0/8, reference Gaussian elimination at 8/8, and complete canonical-key invariance tests.

The only incomplete requirement is external oracle hardening. All three harness runs returned OpenRouter HTTP 403 “Key limit exceeded,” producing zero scored attempts and no valid hardness verdict. The files record this honestly; no `REJECTED.md` was created because this is infrastructure failure, not a G/H/V failure.
