-n-bit certificate language, and the in-context XOR-RHS vote recognizes blocks
-but ignores their coupling. All are rerun across eight shipping seeds. The
-successful elimination algorithm is disclosed under reference_algorithm,
-never misreported as a failed attack.
+Planting hygiene and attacks. Every parity row, core or decoy, is rendered by
+the same four-clause truth table; within every block each variable occurs
+positively twice and negatively twice. Variables and clauses are independently
+relabelled and shuffled. Literal majority, occurrence outliers, public-order
+periodicity, bounded greedy repair, random restarts, and an uncoupled parity-
+RHS vote are all tested over eight shipping seeds. The pair co-degree signal
+is deliberately present: it is the structural clue needed for the short route,
+not a correlation with the sampled answer bits.
