codex
Implemented a verified Track B generator based on the paper’s Section 4 parity-equation-to-CNF construction. The [paper](https://arxiv.org/abs/0907.4573) was read in full.

Deliverables:

- [gen_0907_4573.py](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/0907.4573/gen_0907_4573.py)
- [selftest_report.json](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/0907.4573/selftest_report.json)
- [README.md](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/0907.4573/README.md)
- [bare transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/0907.4573/llm_loop_transcript.jsonl)
- [hinted transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/0907.4573/g9_hinted_transcript.jsonl)
- [placebo transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/0907.4573/g9_placebo_transcript.jsonl)

Offline results:

- All G1–G9(c) gates pass.
- Exact solution density: \(2^{-80}\).
- Random guesses: 0/200,000.
- Six attacks: 0/8 each.
- Gaussian reference algorithm: 8/8, averaging 411,734 counted operations.
- Compact route: 160 XORs.
- Canonical-key symmetry and diversity tests: 20/20.
- Answer size: 161 characters, 80 elements.

The only incomplete requirement is the scored oracle verdict. All three harness runs were attempted, but OpenRouter returned HTTP 403 “Key limit exceeded (total limit)” on every redraw. The harness-owned error transcripts are preserved; no oracle failure or hardness verdict was fabricated. The result is locally verified but must not yet be called oracle-hardened or submitted.
