The existing module’s mathematics checks out, but I found two audit issues to correct before spending oracle calls: it cites the parity-to-CNF construction as Section 4 even though it is in Section 3’s proof of Theorem 1, and its “random restart” probe is only uniform guessing rather than a restart heuristic. I’m also measuring whether a realistic WalkSAT-style attack breaks the shipping distribution.
