The fixed-length hard preset is now strengthened by shuffling all parity blocks and raising safe decoy crowding to the measured 0/8 local-repair ceiling. Unfortunately, the successful first oracle ladder consumed the available OpenRouter quota; the mandated rerun now receives only HTTP 403 errors. I’ll preserve that fact rather than turn API failures into hardness evidence, and finish the reproducible local gates, reports, and scratch-arm transcripts.
