    14	
    15	[Alon et al., *Solving MAX-r-SAT Above a Tight Lower Bound*](https://arxiv.org/abs/0907.4573) defines an exact $r$-CNF as a multiset of clauses, each containing exactly $r$ distinct literals. For $r=3$, $m$ clauses, and the paper's scaled surplus $k$, the question is whether some truth assignment satisfies at least $(7m+k)/8$ clauses. This family sets $k=m$, so a witness must satisfy every clause.
