codex
A correctness audit found unused structure in the advertised shortcut: both variables in each pair share the same two-bit RHS parity. Caching that parity reduces the true compact cost from \(2n\) to \(3n/2\) XORs. That creates a legal \(n=200\) rung at exactly 300 operations, so the earlier `cap_bound` verdict was premature. I’m correcting the route and giving the harness that one additional in-scope escalation before deciding whether this paper parks or ships.
